From e9f9d576a2f06ff69438ff80f30ceb4d4dd8aecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabil <nabil@cea.fr>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:18:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] macOS ARM64 (Apple Silicon) support

- CMake >= 3.5 required (CMake 4.x, e.g. Homebrew, rejects 3.0)
- @rpath/@loader_path install RPATH on macOS for libs, _KernelBasis and tests
- _KernelBasis Python module: -undefined dynamic_lookup instead of linking libpython
- replace unnamed POSIX semaphores (sem_init, not implemented on macOS) used for
  trace-thread start handshake by dispatch semaphores behind portable helpers
- statically initialise pthread mutexes with PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER
  (zero-filled mutex is invalid on macOS)
- XSI strerror_r on macOS
- missing <clocale>/<cwchar> includes (libc++)
- SWIG >= 4.3: PyInt_FromLong -> PyLong_FromLong
- launcher scripts: 'open' instead of 'xdg-open', DYLD_* env robustness,
  bin/salome/python symlink to configured interpreter on macOS
---
